@*
    The root component: the HTML document every page is rendered into.

    Interactivity is declared per page rather than once here (phase 0 declared it globally on
    <Routes>; phase 2's login page is what forces the change). The login page has to run as static
    server-side rendering, not an interactive circuit: HttpContext.SignInAsync writes a Set-Cookie
    header on the HTTP response, and once a circuit is live that response has already been sent --
    there is nothing left to write the cookie onto. Pages that push live updates (the dashboard, the
    health page) opt into @rendermode="InteractiveServer" individually instead.
*@
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <base href="/" />
    <link rel="icon" href="data:," />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="_content/Gleanvolt.Web/css/site.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="_content/Gleanvolt.Web/lib/uplot/uPlot.min.css" />
    <HeadOutlet />
</head>
<body>
    <Routes />
    <script src="_framework/blazor.web.js"></script>
    <!-- Vendored, not a CDN reference (issue #44): the session charts have to keep rendering during
         an internet outage. See wwwroot/lib/uplot/VENDORED.md. -->
    <script src="_content/Gleanvolt.Web/lib/uplot/uPlot.iife.min.js"></script>
    <script src="_content/Gleanvolt.Web/js/charts.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
